1
00:00:17,049 --> 00:00:21,053
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:22,321 --> 00:00:26,358
For somebody who's not escaping
from prison, it sure feels like
I am.

3
00:00:26,925 --> 00:00:28,393
Well, I'm not going anywhere.

4
00:00:28,393 --> 00:00:30,495
I have time to try and
wedge this thing open.

5
00:00:30,495 --> 00:00:32,164
Should be able to do it in under an hour.

6
00:00:33,498 --> 00:00:35,500
No.  That puts me ahead of schedule.

7
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,302
See, this is why unions were formed.

8
00:00:37,302 --> 00:00:38,937
So, when you get lucky breaks like this,

9
00:00:38,937 --> 00:00:42,708
management doesn't make three seconds
the new standard for opening a welded gate.

10
00:00:42,708 --> 00:00:45,510
Yeah, try following me through
this drainage pipe, flyboy.

11
00:00:45,510 --> 00:00:46,778
I don't think so.

12
00:00:46,778 --> 00:00:47,679
[sighs]

13
00:00:47,979 --> 00:00:50,515
Sadly, I am noticing a pattern here.

14
00:00:50,515 --> 00:00:54,820
I seem to be going back and forth between
wanting nothing more than to get above ground

15
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:57,889
then, once I do, there's something
so bad happening topside

16
00:00:57,889 --> 00:01:01,259
that it makes me wish I was never born
and I go back underground again.

17
00:01:01,259 --> 00:01:02,961
Man, fuck Groundhog Day!

18
00:01:02,961 --> 00:01:04,162
It's getting worse, too.

19
00:01:04,162 --> 00:01:06,631
I'm reasonably certain there's
going to be an active volcano outside

20
00:01:06,631 --> 00:01:07,799
if I do this enough times.

21
00:01:07,799 --> 00:01:09,901
[planes whoosh]
Yeah, okay, see, what's that?

22
00:01:09,901 --> 00:01:11,503
[planes whoosh]
Are they spraying nerve gas?

23
00:01:12,070 --> 00:01:12,471
[turret firing]

24
00:01:12,471 --> 00:01:13,538
[turret firing]
Waaah!

25
00:01:13,538 --> 00:01:14,539
[turret beeping]
COME ON!

26
00:01:14,539 --> 00:01:16,375
[turret beeping]
Why is the drainage pipe that's been welded

27
00:01:16,375 --> 00:01:17,843
[turret beeping]
on one end being guarded?

28
00:01:18,377 --> 00:01:19,277
[turret beeping]
And you're beeping.

29
00:01:19,277 --> 00:01:21,246
That's like a death sentence right there.

30
00:01:23,215 --> 00:01:24,015
Did I get it?

31
00:01:24,483 --> 00:01:25,317
It stopped.

32
00:01:26,017 --> 00:01:27,919
I don't know, I like
to be sure about these things.

33
00:01:30,389 --> 00:01:31,223
Close enough.

34
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:34,025
Okay, so, uh...

35
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:37,229
Watch your step.

36
00:01:39,364 --> 00:01:41,366
Jesus, this is pretty high up.

37
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:42,734
[machine gun fire]

38
00:01:42,734 --> 00:01:44,035
Oh, perfect!

39
00:01:44,035 --> 00:01:44,936
That's good!

40
00:01:44,936 --> 00:01:47,105
I needed something to
take my mind off of death.

41
00:01:48,874 --> 00:01:49,608
Echo!

42
00:01:50,776 --> 00:01:52,411
You know, I have the height
advantage here,

43
00:01:52,411 --> 00:01:55,547
so that means my bullets are traveling
a little faster than yours.

44
00:01:58,784 --> 00:02:00,786
HECU: We'll kick your ass!

45
00:02:00,786 --> 00:02:02,154
What'd you say to me?!

46
00:02:02,154 --> 00:02:03,321
Actually, it doesn't matter.

47
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:07,793
I've got the best comeback of all:

48
00:02:07,793 --> 00:02:08,994
a SPAS-12.

49
00:02:10,328 --> 00:02:10,796
What?

50
00:02:11,229 --> 00:02:11,797
What was that?

51
00:02:12,063 --> 00:02:13,031
Didn't catch that.

52
00:02:13,498 --> 00:02:15,867
Yeah, don't have
anything to say now, do you?

53
00:02:16,268 --> 00:02:19,337
I actually don't hold a grudge against
someone talking trash about me

54
00:02:19,337 --> 00:02:21,173
if they're shot afterwards.

55
00:02:21,173 --> 00:02:23,942
I try to rise above that
and find my own peace.

56
00:02:24,443 --> 00:02:26,344
Damn! I am high up.

57
00:02:26,344 --> 00:02:28,613
I don't even see an obvious way down.

58
00:02:28,613 --> 00:02:31,082
Besides, well, the obvious.

59
00:02:31,450 --> 00:02:33,452
Okay, I think this will do it.

60
00:02:33,452 --> 00:02:34,419
Yuaaah!

61
00:02:34,419 --> 00:02:35,253
Christ...

62
00:02:36,888 --> 00:02:40,358
Oh, man, just one trip up here
and that's all it takes to--

63
00:02:40,358 --> 00:02:42,260
[rock crumbles]

64
00:02:42,994 --> 00:02:44,396
Uh...anyway...

65
00:02:44,896 --> 00:02:49,835
I'm not an anthropologist, but I don't
know any modern cliff-dwelling societies.

66
00:02:49,835 --> 00:02:52,471
I'm sure the first settlers probably
thought it was a good idea

67
00:02:52,471 --> 00:02:54,206
because they have good defense,

68
00:02:54,206 --> 00:02:58,210
but once little Billy starts playing near
the cliff, then there's no more little Billy.

69
00:02:58,210 --> 00:03:02,747
Then little Suzy and little Timmy fall off,
which doesn't help the situation.

70
00:03:02,747 --> 00:03:05,217
I think those societies
are all extinct now.

71
00:03:06,084 --> 00:03:06,751
Waah!

72
00:03:06,751 --> 00:03:07,652
Whuuuahh!

73
00:03:07,652 --> 00:03:08,220
Whuuuh...

74
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:10,856
Oh, man that was so sneaky of you.

75
00:03:10,856 --> 00:03:13,391
Getting me to kill you so that
the kickback from my gun

76
00:03:13,391 --> 00:03:15,327
could've knocked me over the edge.

77
00:03:15,327 --> 00:03:16,761
That was clever.

78
00:03:16,761 --> 00:03:19,464
If I hadn't braced myself,
it might've worked.

79
00:03:19,464 --> 00:03:22,834
So, I guess you're just hiding
in a hole in the rock, huh?

80
00:03:22,834 --> 00:03:25,504
Were those your orders, or was
that your own initiative?

81
00:03:25,504 --> 00:03:26,705
Oh, man.

82
00:03:29,674 --> 00:03:31,643
Where are you guys coming from?

83
00:03:33,678 --> 00:03:36,781
If you're trying to do the same
trick as the last guy, you're doing it wrong.

84
00:03:36,781 --> 00:03:38,416
It doesn't work at your angle.

85
00:03:38,416 --> 00:03:41,052
At best, I'll only get knocked
back towards the wall.

86
00:03:41,052 --> 00:03:43,321
I don't know why I'm even
explaining this to you.

87
00:03:43,321 --> 00:03:46,491
Hm, I'm really tempted to slide
down that pipe like a banister

88
00:03:46,491 --> 00:03:49,261
but I think I'll regret it as
soon as I get to the end of it.

89
00:03:49,261 --> 00:03:50,662
I'll find another way.

90
00:03:51,162 --> 00:03:53,698
Seriously, how are these
soldiers getting here?

91
00:03:53,698 --> 00:03:57,335
Parts of this trail are narrow
enough that I'm afraid to sneeze.

92
00:03:57,335 --> 00:04:00,005
Yet, they're sprinkled all over
and stuck in rocks.

93
00:04:00,005 --> 00:04:03,275
Maybe they're still recruits and
this the last part of their training.

94
00:04:03,275 --> 00:04:04,910
And Command just dumps them out of a plane

95
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:06,978
and tells them to make
their way back to base.

96
00:04:06,978 --> 00:04:11,883
No actual plan as to how they're supposed
to get off a cliff. Just ingenuity.

97
00:04:11,883 --> 00:04:14,986
Whoever doesn't die in the
process passes the training.

98
00:04:14,986 --> 00:04:17,289
If two-thirds of the recruits
die or get stranded,

99
00:04:17,289 --> 00:04:19,658
then it's labeled as "intensive training".

100
00:04:19,658 --> 00:04:22,561
I bet there's a bunch more of
these guys stuck in the canyon below.

101
00:04:23,194 --> 00:04:24,029
All right...

102
00:04:24,029 --> 00:04:29,668
This looks like our best
candidate for not...dy-uhhhh...

103
00:04:30,936 --> 00:04:34,205
Okay, careful descent... no
breakdancing moves.

104
00:04:34,205 --> 00:04:35,407
Here we go.

105
00:04:35,407 --> 00:04:38,743
Daaahh! Dah-dah-dah-dah-dah-dah-
dah-dah-dah...

106
00:04:38,743 --> 00:04:39,844
[exhales]

107
00:04:39,844 --> 00:04:41,413
Good to be on this...

108
00:04:42,013 --> 00:04:43,648
THIS ISN'T A PATH!

109
00:04:43,648 --> 00:04:44,583
[growls]

110
00:04:44,583 --> 00:04:46,952
If I'm going the wrong way,
I have problems.

111
00:04:46,952 --> 00:04:48,019
Oh, whoa!

112
00:04:48,019 --> 00:04:50,956
Okay, I think I've
determined the cause of death.

113
00:04:50,956 --> 00:04:51,756
That's two of them.

114
00:04:51,756 --> 00:04:54,426
Maybe hiding in holes really
were their orders.

115
00:04:54,426 --> 00:04:55,594
Why?

116
00:04:55,594 --> 00:04:57,662
Yeah, I'm not getting gun out.

117
00:04:58,396 --> 00:05:00,665
Uhh...huhh...

118
00:05:00,665 --> 00:05:07,038
[whimpering]

119
00:05:07,038 --> 00:05:07,806
Aaah!

120
00:05:08,239 --> 00:05:10,408
If the soldiers wanted to kill
me, they could've just dumped

121
00:05:10,408 --> 00:05:12,510
a bucket of gravel right here.

122
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:13,111
Dead.

123
00:05:13,511 --> 00:05:17,015
I guess I shouldn't be thinking about that,
but I'm pretty sure they can't read my mind.

124
00:05:17,582 --> 00:05:18,283
WAAAAH!

125
00:05:19,417 --> 00:05:21,519
Hell, I can't read my mind.

126
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,623
Wait... maybe.

127
00:05:24,623 --> 00:05:28,793
Speaking of mind-reading, one thing that
pisses me off are those tinfoil hat people.

128
00:05:28,793 --> 00:05:30,629
They don't know what
they're talking about.

129
00:05:30,629 --> 00:05:31,997
Hold on, I've got to
concentrate.

130
00:05:31,997 --> 00:05:33,231
Make sure I don't die.

131
00:05:33,231 --> 00:05:34,366
I do that sometimes.

132
00:05:35,433 --> 00:05:36,534
EEHHH!

133
00:05:36,534 --> 00:05:39,537
[exhales]

134
00:05:39,537 --> 00:05:44,876
But, yeah, assuming mind-reading is
possible--which is big assumption--then...

135
00:05:46,244 --> 00:05:47,646
What the fuck is this?

136
00:05:48,179 --> 00:05:51,549
Is this seriously the bridge
to the other side?

137
00:05:51,549 --> 00:05:55,553
I'd expect better than this from
a Peruvian burrow trail.

138
00:05:55,553 --> 00:05:59,491
Jesus Christ!  Why not just put
up a sign that says, "Die"?

139
00:05:59,491 --> 00:06:02,661
What the fuck?  These pipes
look professionally built.

140
00:06:02,661 --> 00:06:04,129
How did that happen?

141
00:06:04,129 --> 00:06:05,630
Not like this!

142
00:06:05,630 --> 00:06:08,099
The wood's rotting, the
stakes look rusted...

143
00:06:08,099 --> 00:06:11,369
I don't know how the soldiers got
here, but it wasn't this way.

144
00:06:11,369 --> 00:06:14,406
Or, maybe it was; that's why so
many of the planks are missing.

145
00:06:14,406 --> 00:06:19,210
If I had a grappling hook, I could just
tie off, rappel down, and be done with it.

146
00:06:19,210 --> 00:06:20,645
Actually, maybe not.

147
00:06:20,645 --> 00:06:23,048
I'd have to be carrying
a hell of a lot of rope.

148
00:06:23,048 --> 00:06:24,482
[growls]

149
00:06:24,482 --> 00:06:27,585
Well, they did use aircraft
cable; I'll give them that.

150
00:06:27,585 --> 00:06:29,788
So, there's more support if
I walk on the sides,

151
00:06:29,788 --> 00:06:33,425
since the boards look like they
have the tensile-strength of rice cakes.

152
00:06:33,425 --> 00:06:34,893
I'm probably overreacting.

153
00:06:34,893 --> 00:06:37,529
OH NO, IT'SHAPPENINGAAAAAYAAHHHH!

154
00:06:37,529 --> 00:06:48,540
[breathing heavily]

155
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:53,611
In retrospect, maybe I should've checked
to see if the soldiers had any rope on them.

156
00:06:53,611 --> 00:06:55,780
I could've tied at the bridge and...

157
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:57,982
But wait, look at these stakes.

158
00:06:57,982 --> 00:07:00,351
They're practically on
the edge of the rock.

159
00:07:00,351 --> 00:07:02,087
They could've just popped out.

160
00:07:02,887 --> 00:07:05,557
Well, at least no one's following me.

161
00:07:07,358 --> 00:07:09,427
[rocks crumble]

162
00:07:09,427 --> 00:07:11,996
Unless the cliff is following me.

163
00:07:12,997 --> 00:07:14,899
No, that'd be a lot louder.

164
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:19,537
Actually, I'm going to use the pistol;
this is kind of unwieldly right now.

165
00:07:19,537 --> 00:07:21,106
I'm so high up...

166
00:07:21,106 --> 00:07:25,176
I didn't realize Black Mesa was
literally built into the mesa.

167
00:07:25,176 --> 00:07:29,013
I guess that makes my Indian
Burial Ground theory less likely.

168
00:07:29,013 --> 00:07:32,050
I'll take that...

169
00:07:33,752 --> 00:07:35,086
Oh wow.

170
00:07:35,086 --> 00:07:38,022
Yeah, I'm going to trust this
catwalk with my life.

171
00:07:38,022 --> 00:07:42,961
Because, I'm sure it's different from every
other catwalk I've walked on at this company.

172
00:07:42,961 --> 00:07:44,829
Actually, it is different.

173
00:07:44,829 --> 00:07:46,965
The other ones had guardrails.

174
00:07:46,965 --> 00:07:48,833
I think I'll stick with the rock.

175
00:07:48,833 --> 00:07:51,436
At least I know it's been built to code.

176
00:07:52,570 --> 00:07:55,874
If a spider jumps on me now, I'm going
to have to be careful not to freak out.

177
00:07:55,874 --> 00:07:57,242
I could fall off.

178
00:07:57,242 --> 00:07:59,778
I don't think there are many
spiders out here, though.

179
00:07:59,778 --> 00:08:01,146
HECU: Move in!
Wait, you're not a spider.

180
00:08:01,146 --> 00:08:03,248
Okay, careful!  I could fall off!

181
00:08:03,248 --> 00:08:03,948
Careful!

182
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:06,618
What the hell are you doing?!

183
00:08:07,218 --> 00:08:09,320
I could slip on these shells!

184
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:10,755
You ever think of that?!

185
00:08:10,755 --> 00:08:12,524
No!  Of course not!

186
00:08:12,524 --> 00:08:15,527
As usual, I'm the one who has to
think of these things.

187
00:08:16,761 --> 00:08:18,997
Whoa-ho!  Motion-sensor doors.

188
00:08:18,997 --> 00:08:21,533
This is a step up from the
death-slide trail.

189
00:08:22,433 --> 00:08:23,234
Is that...?

190
00:08:24,235 --> 00:08:26,004
Oh my God, it's a rocket launcher.

191
00:08:26,971 --> 00:08:29,741
The perfect gift for the
man who has everything.

192
00:08:30,642 --> 00:08:34,445
Ooooh... you and I are gonna go places.

193
00:08:34,445 --> 00:08:38,082
My mind is spinning with new possibilities.

194
00:08:38,082 --> 00:08:42,153
You are the first
good news I've had all day.

195
00:08:42,153 --> 00:08:43,922
Yes, I'll bring your friends.

196
00:08:44,823 --> 00:08:45,456
[lock jiggles]

197
00:08:45,456 --> 00:08:46,157
Locked!

198
00:08:46,791 --> 00:08:47,559
[helicopter whirring]
Hark!

199
00:08:47,559 --> 00:08:51,663
[helicopter whirring]
Dost thou hear with thine ears
what I hear with mine?

200
00:08:51,663 --> 00:08:52,997
[helicopter whirring]
Interloper!

201
00:08:52,997 --> 00:08:56,100
No quarter shall be shown
hither, fiend!

202
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:58,570
Anon!  Show thineself, churl!

203
00:09:00,171 --> 00:09:00,738
Have at thee!

204
00:09:01,472 --> 00:09:03,107
[helicopter firing]

205
00:09:03,107 --> 00:09:04,409
BLACKGUARD!  AAH!

206
00:09:05,443 --> 00:09:06,911
FIE UPON ME!

207
00:09:06,911 --> 00:09:07,745
But ho!

208
00:09:07,745 --> 00:09:12,383
The laser on mine rocket launcher be not
a mere target, but a guidance system.

209
00:09:12,383 --> 00:09:13,918
Where art thou?!

210
00:09:13,918 --> 00:09:16,154
Come hither that I may smite thee!

211
00:09:21,326 --> 00:09:23,962
Thou shalt not be missed.

212
00:09:23,962 --> 00:09:25,663
That was liberating.

213
00:09:25,663 --> 00:09:27,599
Whoa, wait, what's that sound?

214
00:09:27,599 --> 00:09:28,600
Do you hear that?

215
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,134
I think that's silence!

216
00:09:30,134 --> 00:09:33,872
THAT'S THE SOUND PEOPLE MAKE WHEN
EVERYONE TRYING TO KILL ME IS DEAD!

217
00:09:33,872 --> 00:09:35,940
AND I HAVE A ROCKET LAUNCHER!

218
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:39,711
I HAVE A ROCKET LAUNCHER WITH A
LASER-GUIDANCE SYSTEM!

219
00:09:39,711 --> 00:09:43,314
And...I'm walking on... a really...

220
00:09:43,314 --> 00:09:44,682
...really...

221
00:09:44,682 --> 00:09:46,684
...narrow cliff-face.

222
00:09:46,684 --> 00:09:47,585
Wuuahhh...

223
00:09:48,253 --> 00:09:49,053
Hmm.

224
00:09:49,053 --> 00:09:51,522
Besides seeming like a gift from the gods,

225
00:09:51,522 --> 00:09:54,058
this rocket launcher gives me
some food for thought.

226
00:09:54,058 --> 00:09:58,496
I may have to revise my theory
about the universe wanting me dead.

227
00:09:58,496 --> 00:10:01,866
If that was true, the rocket
launcher would never have happened.

228
00:10:01,866 --> 00:10:04,969
Only most of the universe wants me dead.

229
00:10:04,969 --> 00:10:07,105
There's some larger game going on here.

230
00:10:07,105 --> 00:10:13,077
I'm more like Perseus or Odysseus
caught in the center of some cosmic politics.

231
00:10:13,077 --> 00:10:16,648
That's too bad; I was hoping the
universe would end with me.

232
00:10:16,648 --> 00:10:18,716
Maybe there's still a way to
make that happen.

233
00:10:19,550 --> 00:10:20,451
Hmm.

234
00:10:20,451 --> 00:10:22,654
I feel like I'm forgetting
something important.

235
00:10:23,988 --> 00:10:25,890
Mind reading!  That was it.

236
00:10:25,890 --> 00:10:27,458
Okay, let's assume it exists,

237
00:10:27,458 --> 00:10:30,561
even though the transmission doesn't
show up on any known spectrum.

238
00:10:31,095 --> 00:10:32,664
The tinfoil hat people.

239
00:10:32,664 --> 00:10:33,698
What do they think?

240
00:10:34,299 --> 00:10:37,001
That it's electromagnetic radiation?

241
00:10:37,001 --> 00:10:39,203
Then what do they think
the tin is going to do?

242
00:10:39,737 --> 00:10:40,672
Whuh-huh-AHHHH!

243
00:10:40,772 --> 00:10:41,205
AAAAHHH!

244
00:10:41,372 --> 00:10:41,839
AAAAHHH!

245
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:42,540
AAAAHHH!

246
00:10:42,941 --> 00:10:43,374
AAAHH!

247
00:10:43,841 --> 00:10:44,309
AAH!

248
00:10:44,909 --> 00:10:45,310
Ah...

249
00:10:45,944 --> 00:10:47,111
[whimpers]

250
00:10:47,111 --> 00:10:49,747
Th-that-that step was a little tricky.

251
00:10:49,747 --> 00:10:52,116
Oh God...oh God!

252
00:10:52,116 --> 00:10:54,018
Oooohhh...

253
00:10:54,018 --> 00:10:58,022
So, anyway, if it's electromagnetic,
you'd need a Faraday Cage to block that

254
00:10:58,022 --> 00:11:00,491
and a tinfoil hat doesn't act like one.

255
00:11:00,491 --> 00:11:01,592
It's not even grounded.

256
00:11:01,592 --> 00:11:03,861
In all likelihood, a chunk of
metal on your head

257
00:11:03,861 --> 00:11:07,765
is going to conduct any signal
you're worried about, not block it.

258
00:11:07,765 --> 00:11:10,702
You'd have better chances with a
lead helmet coated in rubber.

259
00:11:10,702 --> 00:11:12,670
Tinfoil hat people are ignorant.

260
00:11:12,670 --> 00:11:13,304
[headcrab squeals]

261
00:11:13,304 --> 00:11:14,973
OH GOD!  JESUS!

262
00:11:14,973 --> 00:11:15,873
[headcrab squeals]

263
00:11:15,873 --> 00:11:18,176
YEAH!  TORO, MOTHERFUCKER!

264
00:11:19,143 --> 00:11:20,378
Splat!

265
00:11:22,513 --> 00:11:25,516
Forget the mind-reading
I just want a helmet.

266
00:11:25,516 --> 00:11:29,053
Cranial protection against
punctures and lacerations.

267
00:11:29,721 --> 00:11:30,855
And bullets.

268
00:11:32,991 --> 00:11:33,891
Hmm.

269
00:11:33,891 --> 00:11:35,727
Well, I'm not wasting
a rocket on the chance

270
00:11:35,727 --> 00:11:38,730
that there might be another one
of those things in here.

271
00:11:38,730 --> 00:11:42,133
I guess I'll just do things the
potentially painful way.

272
00:11:45,536 --> 00:11:47,071
If the circumstances were different,

273
00:11:47,071 --> 00:11:50,634
this area would actually be a pretty
kick-ass place to build a waterslide.

